<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dutch colonial empire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dutch Empire was the overseas colonial and commercial empire of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, built mainly from the seventeenth century by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>. Centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>, it also included trading posts and colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, and it lasted in part into the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-empire.jpg" alt="Dutch Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miyamaki, Oren neu dag, Artem Karimov, Golradir · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prinsenvlag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
